From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:43:55 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 60/63] misc: samsung: scsc: build the WLBT core on 6.18

Add a reduced Kconfig/Makefile (Exynos 9610 platform interface, core
manager and the NULL-service test client only) and adapt the imported
4.14 sources to 6.18, using current kernel interfaces:

- firmware and configuration files are requested by bare name through
  the firmware loader (6.11+ refuses ".." names, so the 5.4-era
  "../etc/wifi" trick is gone); CONFIG_SCSC_CORE_FW_LOCATION must be in
  firmware_class.path. No set_fs/vfs_stat, no VFS-internal namespace.
- shared memory comes from the "memory-region" phandle at probe instead
  of a global RESERVEDMEM_OF_DECLARE hook.
- interrupts by name with platform_get_irq_byname() (OF no longer
  provides IRQ resources); trigger type from the DT.
- the EL3 connectivity SiP call (SMC_CMD_CONN_IF, set TZPC non-secure)
  uses arm_smccc_smc().
- proc_ops/pde_data, timespec64, strscpy, devm_ioremap, class_create()
  without owner, void platform remove.
- CONFIG_SOC_EXYNOS9610 becomes CONFIG_SCSC_PLATFORM_EXYNOS9610.
- the exynos_soc_info revision was only logged on 9610 (mxconf gets it
  only for 7885); the log line is dropped.
- the mif debug procfs (memory dump/write, register read) and the dead
  bitmap debug print are not built.

Not ported: PCIe, logring (messages go to printk), log collection, PM QoS,
smapper, wlbtd, mxlogger, ANT, FM and the other debug devices. Wakelocks
stay compiled out (no CONFIG_ANDROID); suspend is outside this step.

Change-Id: I7c8899dd4abf324bda4c7db0d0328c0533defd30
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
